diagnosis_text:
A thorough multi-layer investigation found no network-side fault affecting PC11 (172.16.20.11). Phase 1 reachability probes showed PC11 successfully reaching cross-subnet destinations pc6 (172.16.10.6) and pc1 (10.5.0.1) with 0% loss. Phase A infrastructure sweep confirmed PC11 has the correct IPv4 address (172.16.20.11/24) and default gateway (172.16.20.254), with no ACL/firewall rules, no duplicate MAC, and no static ARP poisoning on any device in the lab. Phase B showed the OSPF routing fabric fully converged across all nine routers with 18 routes apiece, and no traffic-control shaping on any interface. Phase D pressure sweep found no stress tools, CPU overload, or resource contention on any device. Direct targeted pings between PC11 and its same-VLAN-20 neighbour PC10 succeeded in both directions at sub-millisecond latency, with zero packet loss — confirming local-subnet connectivity is intact. PC11's eth0 interface is UP/LOWER_UP with zero receive/transmit errors and zero carrier changes. The DHCP/link history helper found no suspicious events on PC11. There is no flap script, no carrier-transition history, no disrupted DHCP lease, and no routing or addressing misconfiguration anywhere in the topology. The reported symptom — PC11 unable to reach any host, including adjacent VLAN-20 machines — is entirely contradicted by live network evidence. The network has not dropped PC11; the device is fully operational and reachable from all sampled peers.
=== END ===